From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: no App Nap while the VM runs

What: QEMU's window process holds an NSProcessInfo activity
(NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep) from the start of its run
loop; OMACVM_APP_NAP=1 leaves it out. QEMU's log says which.

Why: macOS naps an app none of whose windows can be seen: the screen
locked, the VM's full screen on another Space, the window minimized or
covered. A napped QEMU runs every thread (vCPUs, main loop) at background
priority 4 and the guest crawls. Measured on an M4 Max, screen locked,
4 vCPUs busy in the guest (python loop counter, 40 s): 10-100 million
loops/s napped, 490-590 with the activity (as with a visible window); all
QEMU threads at priority 4 napped, 28-31 with it. UTM's QEMU (a helper without
windows) and Parallels' VM process are never napped. The Mac can still
sleep when idle (AllowingIdleSystemSleep).

Upstream: not sent (QEMU's cocoa UI is for a desktop window; a policy choice).
Test: src/tests/app-nap.sh (offline); QEMU's log line; the live check in
the test's header (vCPU thread priority with the window out of sight).

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -4260,8 +4260,33 @@
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM: no App Nap. macOS naps an app when none of its windows can be seen
+ * (the screen locked, the VM's full screen on another Space, the window
+ * minimized or covered): every QEMU thread drops to background priority and
+ * the guest runs at 2-20 % of its speed (measured on an M4 Max with the
+ * screen locked: 4 busy vCPUs did 10-100 instead of ~550 million loops/s). A
+ * VM keeps working while nobody looks at it, as in UTM or Parallels. Idle
+ * system sleep stays allowed. OMACVM_APP_NAP=1 lets macOS nap it (tests).
+ */
+static void omacvm_no_app_nap(void)
+{
+    static id activity;
+    const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_APP_NAP");
+
+    if (v && strcmp(v, "1") == 0) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: App Nap: allowed (OMACVM_APP_NAP=1)");
+        return;
+    }
+    activity = [[[NSProcessInfo processInfo]
+        beginActivityWithOptions:NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep
+                          reason:@"the virtual machine runs"] retain];
+    info_report("OmacVM: App Nap: off while the VM runs");
+}
+
 static int cocoa_main(void)
 {
+    omacvm_no_app_nap();
     COCOA_DEBUG("Main thread: entering OSX run loop\n");
     [NSApp run];
     COCOA_DEBUG("Main thread: left OSX run loop, which should never happen\n");
